/* FillArray_r: intermediate level of FillArray, written by hand (PipelineB, refinement step), the
   component BART refines.
   Purpose: replace the lambda of set_array_value by the facts a loop establishes: the new array is a
   total function, and each position holds its own number. The proof that these facts define the
   lambda (equality of two functions) is thus done once, here, away from the loop.
   array stays the concrete variable of FillArray, and its initialisation is unchanged.
   Two choices follow Quicksort_r, the only level with an inherited concrete variable BART has
   refined:
   - an INVARIANT clause, restating the type of array. Without it, BART stopped silently on this
     level, twice;
   - an ANY, taken by a structure rule, in place of array :( ... ) on the variable itself. */
REFINEMENT
    FillArray_r

REFINES
    FillArray

SEES
    Ctx_FillArray

INVARIANT
    array : (0..max_IDX) --> INT

INITIALISATION
    array := (0..max_IDX) * {0}

OPERATIONS

    set_array_value =
    ANY rr WHERE
        rr : (0..max_IDX) --> INT &
        !ii.(ii : 0..max_IDX => rr(ii) = ii)
    THEN
        array := rr
    END

END
